{"user": "I don't quite follow (I've never played this game before)", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T15:00:17.561353+00:00", "assistant": "No worries.\n\nBasic idea: when Black plays, you flip White discs only if they\u2019re **sandwiched in a straight line** between your new disc and another black disc.\n\nBut near the end, the key is not \u201chow many flip now\u201d \u2014 it\u2019s:\n\n- **Corners** like **a8** are permanent once taken.\n- Squares next to a corner can accidentally help White get that corner.\n- A move is strong if it leaves White with **few or no legal moves**.\n\nSo for **c8**, don\u2019t just count the flips. Ask: *after c8, what can White do near the open a8 corner?* That corner may matter more than 4 flipped discs.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T15:00:30.849976+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T15:00:33.063472+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Metacomment"], "votes": {"Metacomment": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Metacomment": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Metacomment"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "sonnet": ["Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 2, "Prompt": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Prompt": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Prompt"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hi